  "Question": "A figure is an equiangular parallelogram if and only if it is a",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "rectangle",
    "B": "regular polygon",
    "C": "rhombus",
    "D": "square",
    "E": "trapezoid"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Equiangular means that all the interior angles are equal. Adjacent angles of a parallelogram sum to \\(180^\\circ\\), because its opposite sides are parallel. If those adjacent angles are equal, each is\n\\[\n180^\\circ\\div2=90^\\circ.\n\\]\nA parallelogram with a right angle is a rectangle.\n\nConversely, every rectangle is a parallelogram with four right angles, so it is equiangular. Both directions hold, so the answer is rectangle, choice \\(\\text{A}\\).",
